                            <p><strong style="color: var(--text-main);">Dry Run:</strong> Builds the final bash script explicitly in mock mode. It aggressively asserts all SSH connections and pre-checks exist, but <b>will not</b> actually stream your production files over `rsync` or do heavy `pg_dump` databases extracts. Always generate your first run with this checked to test your IPs!</p>
                            <p style="margin-top: 8px;"><strong style="color: var(--text-main);">Maint Mode (DB Locks):</strong> Primarily used for resolving Database-tier delta diffs. Executes your specific <i>App Read-Only CMD</i> string directly on the Source OSPC nodes right before file-syncing begins. Use this to safely lock your Application so that no real web users make new database account creation writes that would otherwise get lost in the transition gap!</p>
                            <p style="margin-top: 8px;"><strong style="color: var(--text-main);">Cutover Mode (Cold Transfer):</strong> Programs the script to dynamically utilize Linux `systemctl` bindings internally to gracefully <b>stop</b> the Backend API and web nodes on the OSPC platform so that log files and static assets are fully idle and safe to Rsync copy, and then automatically restarts those services on your new FLEX host targets!</p>
